  "card": "PR #34778 rewrites logging macros in util/log.h to route through a single LOG_EMIT macro taking compile-time options. It enforces logging category rules at compile time via static assertions, eliminating cryptic compiler syntax errors when categories are omitted or misplaced. It also avoids message formatting when logging is disabled while preserving argument evaluation semantics for high-severity logs, and cleans up rate-limiting parameter plumbing. This is an internal developer refactoring that also serves as a base for kernel and wallet logging improvements in PR #30342 and PR #30343.",
